Data types
Primitive data types - includes byte, short, int, long, float, double, boolean and char
Non-primitive data types - such as String, Arrays and Classes

public static void main(String[] args) {
    System.out.println("Hello!");
}

public → The method can be accessed from anywhere. The JVM needs to be able to call it.
static → The method belongs to the class, so Java can run it without creating an object.
void → The method does not return any value.
main → The special method name Java looks for as the program's entry point.
String[] args → An array that stores command-line arguments passed to the program.

